{"title":"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Informal)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Informal)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde1774a06facbf7b3c05e82bc4ed9bd41cd786a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96fe6ca9907a547c4fbb1ae61dc66345febe7ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6445200e3dcd16169cbc6bc19d8c14173de439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb0f1d8a43539dbc3355734bafb2bfd855b5f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece071fd3240cd4f6870b9e64a3f9b38387a09bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=p\\cdot AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf69682047225108ceae7099724871699f9ace14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=q\\cdot BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/b/28bb2c2ee70c95d46e49f395062cc470e040f45f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF=r\\cdot CA$\" width=\"102\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive and satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee7bb38c464dd7d6dd8b7391b862459c635c3a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r=\\frac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16dc9005ef9271d7be329fc1472397f31898388b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+q^2+r^2=\\frac25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />. The ratio of the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> to the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a> positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa532b18510960c694fe8213246465f219c7d942.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  /* -- arbitrary values, I couldn&#39;t find nice values for pqr please replace if possible -- */  real p = 0.5, q = 0.1, r = 0.05;   /* -- arbitrary values, I couldn&#39;t find nice values for pqr please replace if possible -- */  pointpen = black; pathpen = linewidth(0.7) + black; pair A=(0,0),B=(13,0),C=IP(CR(A,17),CR(B,15)), D=A+p*(B-A), E=B+q*(C-B), F=C+r*(A-C); D(D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A))--D(MP(&quot;B&quot;,B))--D(MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,N))--cycle); D(D(MP(&quot;D&quot;,D))--D(MP(&quot;E&quot;,E,NE))--D(MP(&quot;F&quot;,F,NW))--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"215\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710131907cfe6ede3e2195a1a5c68cffb5b203f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\ldots]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> denote area; then the desired value is \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f031606bd0480fc8cb6ee9da5a70ec5dccdfcecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac mn = \\frac{[DEF]}{[ABC]} = \\frac{[ABC] - [ADF] - [BDE] - [CEF]}{[ABC]}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"410\" height=\"43\" /></center>\n<p>Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle#Related_Formulae_and_Theorems\" title=\"Triangle\">formula</a> for the area of a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/9/4b962645287def711ea0f0c94e40c1e563aab6b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" />, we find that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc254e39ee583e6f0e7845a84cb9f1e473868472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[ADF]}{[ABC]} = \\frac{\\frac 12 \\cdot p \\cdot AB \\cdot (1-r) \\cdot AC \\cdot \\sin \\angle CAB}{\\frac 12 \\cdot AB \\cdot AC \\cdot \\sin \\angle CAB} = p(1-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"448\" height=\"47\" /></center>\n<p>and similarly that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314ac41a75f721b95a9cc9154ec38dc920614ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[BDE]}{[ABC]} = q(1-p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"144\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f38dafeb4a3f76d640a9f865c68e5a6f001de43a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{[CEF]}{[ABC]} = r(1-q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"142\" height=\"43\" />. Thus, we wish to find \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38a66c816b5f7aede400644c7f710603718a56f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\frac{[DEF]}{[ABC]} &amp;= 1 - \\frac{[ADF]}{[ABC]} - \\frac{[BDE]}{[ABC]} - \\frac{[CEF]}{[ABC]}  \\\\ &amp;= 1 - p(1-r) - q(1-p) - r(1-q)\\\\ &amp;= (pq + qr + rp) - (p + q + r) + 1 \\end{align*}\" width=\"344\" height=\"93\" />\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc13782734a477c83d3f177c85f1241bb7745ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q + r = \\frac 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"108\" height=\"37\" />, and also that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/587d06deafed5ae8bf561044f837617fc9c5491d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p+q+r)^2 = p^2 + q^2 + r^2 + 2(pq + qr + rp) \\Longleftrightarrow pq + qr + rp = \\frac{\\left(\\frac 23\\right)^2 - \\frac 25}{2} = \\frac{1}{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"634\" height=\"45\" />. Substituting, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e58cd679413fe6cd0cb5868eef48ed28c5adc9ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1{45} - \\frac 23 + 1 = \\frac{16}{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1079337c1ed25c907c12f92357c99fff57e24d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{061}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By the barycentric area formula, our desired ratio is equal to \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf0407d6a43ecb4ac0588afe8a1274e1760f31c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\begin{vmatrix} 1-p &amp; p &amp; 0 \\\\  0 &amp; 1-q &amp; q  \\\\  r &amp; 0 &amp; 1-r \\notag \\end{vmatrix} &amp;=1-p-q-r+pq+qr+pr\\\\ &amp;=1-(p+q+r)+\\frac{(p+q+r)^2-(p^2+q^2+r^2)}{2}\\\\ &amp;=1-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{2}{5}}{2}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{16}{45}, \\end{align*}\" width=\"550\" height=\"200\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/67011f852e18a5c927e5dbc7765491bb88da153f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{061}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Informal.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Informal)\">Solution 3 (Informal)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Informal)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since the only conditions are that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d5b1ec1efc6d51e08d13b62ba52f2d5b1efd4cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q + r = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/b/b1b9e62cf6841629e9a025ac6c302584011e9bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 + q^2 + r^2 = \\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />, we can simply let one of the variables be equal to 0. In this case, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/868c0cce47ca5e001d017eaf95b3a9b31c7b292e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c315d35745c151284943a9ee2eb820a807cd2d96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q + r = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d0bf35e77f563cdfc4f4eba17b1fef06b144012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2 + r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2297526ede0e6c616802ca72adf69c82518f25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Note that the ratio between the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a906aed771372478b201cdf46b9420873f89a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-q)(1-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />. Solving this system of equations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259ab212ea58456f651630b8cdcd25a7e5be2b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = \\frac{1}{3} \\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{45}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"110\" height=\"45\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01c3f208a96f273aabb51f2552287bc16ae6c27b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{1}{3} \\mp \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{45}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"110\" height=\"45\" />. Plugging back into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a906aed771372478b201cdf46b9420873f89a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-q)(1-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/615039604273c377b1692de47c99460a09e8e109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/67011f852e18a5c927e5dbc7765491bb88da153f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{061}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Because the givens in the problem statement are all regarding the ratios of the sides, the side lengths of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c9118304bd04a08831b673f02f0085df6f8547ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13, 15, 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />, are actually not necessary to solve the problem. This is clearly demonstrated in all of the above solutions, as the side lengths are not used at all.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I\" title=\"2001 AIME I\">2001 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2001\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2001 AIME I Problems/Problem 